  "published": "2026-11-07T10:21:35.047Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v17.3.2 / v18.3.2: Version lines now follow the Umbraco major (17.x for Umbraco 17, 18.x for Umbraco 18) and each line's Umbraco.Cms.Api.Management dependency is boxed to a single major - [17.0.0, 18.0.0) and [18.0.0, 19.0.0) respectively. Previously a single net10.0 build declared [17.0.0, 19.0.0), which let a host pinned to Umbraco 17 be pulled up to Umbraco 18 whenever another package in the project graph demanded 18. Boxing the range per major prevents that cross-major drift: installing into an Umbraco 17 site always resolves the 17.x line and never forces an 18 upgrade. Umbraco 16 (the old net9.0 target) is no longer supported. No functional, API, UI or database changes - this is a packaging/compatibility change only. v3.2.0: Fetch history and mobile/desktop compare. Every completed fetch is recorded in a new history list (re-run past fetches with one click, clear anytime, capped at 200 rows, HTML bodies are never stored); the new Compare Mobile/Desktop button fetches the URL as both the smartphone and desktop Googlebot and highlights every differing field (title, meta, word count, noindex, cloaking, SEO and AI-readiness scores). No breaking API changes. v2.0.0: Refactored as a dedicated URL Viewer tool. Site-wide crawler and per-node SEO Audit tab moved to the companion uTPro.Feature.SEOAudit package. Engine extracted to T4VN.Seo.Core (shared by both packages). Adds Lighthouse-style composite SEO score (0â€“100) with per-category sub-scores (SEO / Technical / Content / Accessibility) and individual check pass/fail with remediation advice. Section renamed to match new dedicated role; configuration key changed to uTPro:Feature:UrlViewer.",
